    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass15b03e07_09be_4dff_84a5_7a69f178ed8b -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass15b03e07_09be_4dff_84a5_7a69f178ed8b">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org//Childbearing-ageWomenwithEpilepsyOntology#OWLClass7aa094f9_1233_480b_b8b2_466e1c3e8d44"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>激素替代治疗</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>Therapeutic use of hormones to alleviate the effects of hormone deficiency.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>Treatment with estrogens or estrogen/progesterone after menopause or ovariectomy to prevent pathological effects of decreased estrogen production.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NICE_guidance>Refer to the SPC and BNF for individual drug advice on the interactions between AEDs and hormonal replacement and contraception.[new 2012]
有关 AED 与激素替代或避孕之间相互作用的个别药物建议，请参阅 SPC 和 BNF。[2012 年新]
nice.org.uk/guidance/cg137</untitled-ontology-34:NICE_guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:D]Hormone replacement therapy should be prescribed for the same indications as in women who do not have epilepsy.
D级推荐：激素替代疗法适应症与一般人群相同。
Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network.Diagnosis and management of epilepsy in adults. SIGN 143. Edinburgh, SIGN, 2015. Available at: www.sign.ac.uk/guidelines/fulltext/143/index.html</untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>
