        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>丙泊酚</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>An intravenous anesthetic agent which has the advantage of a very rapid onset after infusion or bolus injection plus a very short recovery period of a couple of minutes. (From Smith and Reynard, Textbook of Pharmacology, 1992, 1st ed, p206). Propofol has been used as ANTICONVULSANTS and ANTIEMETICS.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>A hypnotic alkylphenol derivative. Formulated for intravenous induction of sedation and hypnosis during anesthesia, propofol facilitates inhibitory neurotransmission mediated by gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA). This agent is associated with minimal respiratory depression and has a short half-life with a duration of action of 2 to 10 minutes.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
