Amiodarone (substance)
Methanone (2-butyl-3-benzofuranyl)(4-(2-(diethylamino)ethoxy)-35-diiodophenyl)-
amiodarone
Amiodaronum
2-Butyl-3-benzofuranyl 4-(2-(diethylamino)ethoxy)-35-diiodophenyl ketone
Product containing amiodarone (medicinal product)
2-Butyl-3-(35-diiodo-4-(2-diethylaminoethoxy)benzoyl)benzofuran
Amiodarona</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Amiodarone</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass3a34c329_159a_4dd8_9c6d_2cfcd77f020d -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass3a34c329_159a_4dd8_9c6d_2cfcd77f020d">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9e8550e9_9259_4826_a257_3569677963b0"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>莫雷西嗪</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>An antiarrhythmia agent used primarily for ventricular rhythm disturbances.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Carbamic acid (10-(3-(4-morpholinyl)-1-oxopropyl)-10H-phenothiazin-2-yl)- ethyl ester
moracizine
