    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass4f27d3a3_7013_4343_bce6_115918d87f26 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass4f27d3a3_7013_4343_bce6_115918d87f26">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClasse6f48ae5_1e6f_4d56_ab55_d3032096a737"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>丁螺环酮</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>An anxiolytic agent and serotonin receptor agonist belonging to the azaspirodecanedione class of compounds. Its structure is unrelated to those of the BENZODIAZAPINES, but it has an efficacy comparable to DIAZEPAM.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>An anxiolytic agent chemically and pharmacologically unrelated to benzodiazepines, barbiturates, or other sedative/hypnotic drugs. Although its exact mechanism of action is unknown, buspirone may exert its anti-anxiety effects via serotonin (5-HT1A) and dopamine receptors (D2) and may indirectly affect other neurotransmitter systems. Unlike typical benzodiazepine anxiolytics, this agent does not exert anticonvulsant or muscle relaxant effects and lacks prominent sedative effects.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
