    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass55792ae2_d354_4dc8_ae1d_302495585633 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass55792ae2_d354_4dc8_ae1d_302495585633">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassc27bf42d_b77e_460f_8c7f_45ba0580f229"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>冥想</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>A state of consciousness in which the individual eliminates environmental stimuli from awareness so that the mind can focus on a single thing, producing a state of relaxation and relief from stress. A wide variety of techniques are used to clear the mind of stressful outside interferences. It includes meditation therapy. (Mosby&apos;s Medical, Nursing, and Allied Health Dictionary, 4th ed)</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Meditation
meditation</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Meditation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass563933cc_d685_4d22_92b3_fdf2b679b42f -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass563933cc_d685_4d22_92b3_fdf2b679b42f">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass99b37c58_bf03_4c2f_b353_5c64e4a80a82"/>
        <OWLAnnotationProperty5b4bece4_34a5_4955_86ae_fe5305e84ce9>China_expert_opinion_2015
如果妊娠期间发作控制不佳，需考虑可能与妊娠早期剧烈呕吐、依从性差等所致的血清药物浓度降低有关。应依据患者具体情况采取相应措施。
中国医师协会神经内科分会癫(癎)专委会. &quot;妊娠期女性抗癫(癎)药物应用中国专家共识.&quot; 中国医师杂志 17.7(2015):969-971.</OWLAnnotationProperty5b4bece4_34a5_4955_86ae_fe5305e84ce9>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>血清</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>The clear portion of BLOOD that is left after BLOOD COAGULATION to remove BLOOD CELLS and clotting proteins.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>The clear portion of the blood that remains after the removal of the blood cells and the clotting proteins.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:ROCG_Guidance>[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:C] Based on current evidence, routine monitoring of serum AED levels in pregnancy is not recommended although individual circumstances may be taken into account.
【推荐等级：C】根据目前的证据，不建议常规监测妊娠期AEDs血清浓度。
https://www.rcog.org.uk/guidance/browse-all-guidance/green-top-guidelines/epilepsy-in-pregnancy-green-top-guideline-no-68/</untitled-ontology-34:ROCG_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Serum
Portion of serum
blood serum
SERUM
Serum Blood
Serums
Sera
Blood serum
Serum (substance)
serum
Blood Serum</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Serum</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass567b56fb_d427_427c_88fe_ba3df8a0866d -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass567b56fb_d427_427c_88fe_ba3df8a0866d">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org//Childbearing-ageWomenwithEpilepsyOntology#OWLClassb956c7af_58b2_4cfa_b0e6_5e3a9bffcf7b"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>脑电图</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>Recording of electric currents developed in the brain by means of electrodes applied to the scalp, to the surface of the brain, or placed within the substance of the brain.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>The neurophysiologic exploration of the electrical activity of the brain by the application of electrodes to the scalp. The resulting traces are known as an electroencephalogram (EEG). This test is used to assess brain damage, epilepsy and other problems.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>ELECTROENCEPHALOGRAPHY
EEG
electroencephalogram
Electroencephalogram (procedure)
electroencephalography
Electroencephalography
Electroencephalogram (EEG)
Electroencephalogram
EEG - Electroencephalography
ELECTROENCEPHALOGR</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:comment>脑电图和血药浓度有助于对患者进行管理。VPA血药浓度可以作为指导，但其个体差异很大，缺乏关于母体血药浓度与MCMs风险之间的关系的证据。建议将VPA水平根据临床反应维持在推荐治疗范围以下。脑电图并不是可靠的指标。
Patient management will vary across different national health systems. EEG recordings and plasma drug concentration measurements, for example, may be part of national epilepsy management guidelines. Plasma valproate levels may be used as a guide, but interindividual doses vary widely and defnitive data on the association between maternal plasma drug levels and MCM risks are lacking. The target valproate level can be maintained below the recommended therapeutic range, depending on clinical response. EEG recordings are not a reliable biomarker of clinical response, but they can be of help when interpreted by an epilepsy specialist. Family planning is important in patients taking AEDs. 
Toledo M, Mostacci B, Bosak M, Jedrzejzak J, Thomas RH, Salas-Puig J, Biraben A, Schmitz B. Expert opinion: use of valproate in girls and women of childbearing potential with epilepsy: recommendations and alternatives based on a review of the literature and clinical experience-a European perspective. J Neurol. 2020 Apr 1. doi: 10.1007/s00415-020-09809-0. Epub ahead of print. PMID: 32239268.

Recommendations for valproate switching and discontinuation in girls and WOCP with epilepsy
在更换或停用VPA之前，必须评估血浆VPA水平、患者体重、不良反应和病情严重程度。在换药期间，应加强对患者的管理，并监测/追踪（track）“轻微（minor）”发作（肌阵挛或失神发作）。如果全身性发作能够得到良好的控制，在评估了癫痫发作风险的情况下，轻微的发作可能是可以接受的。连续脑电图记录（包括重复光刺激和过度换气）对特发性全身发作是有用的。在换药期间检测到发作期间癫痫样活动增加（increased interictal epileptiform activity）或光阵发性反应的再现（reappearance of a photoparoxysmal response）表明治疗方案可能需要更改，以防止GTCS突破性发作（breakthrough GTCS）。
Plasma valproate levels, weight, adverse events, and epilepsy severity must all be assessed before switching or stopping valproate. During the switch, patient management should be intensified and “minor” seizures (myoclonic or absence seizures) tracked. Minor seizures may be acceptable when GTCS are well controlled and when the risks of having a seizure are considered (e.g., a car accident). Serial EEG recordings including repetitive photostimulation and hyperventilation maneuvers can be useful in patients with IGE. Detection of increased interictal epileptiform activity or reappearance of a photoparoxysmal response during the switching period may indicate that the treatment needs to revised to prevent breakthrough GTCS.
Toledo M, Mostacci B, Bosak M, Jedrzejzak J, Thomas RH, Salas-Puig J, Biraben A, Schmitz B. Expert opinion: use of valproate in girls and women of childbearing potential with epilepsy: recommendations and alternatives based on a review of the literature and clinical experience-a European perspective. J Neurol. 2020 Apr 1. doi: 10.1007/s00415-020-09809-0. Epub ahead of print. PMID: 32239268.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Electroencephalography</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass571ddf6c_874a_478d_8c4d_6f6f1360a372 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass571ddf6c_874a_478d_8c4d_6f6f1360a372">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassdd746922_f5f4_45b7_9f02_91092fa08d45"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>二甲双胍</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>A biguanide hypoglycemic agent used in the treatment of non-insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus not responding to dietary modification. Metformin improves glycemic control by improving insulin sensitivity and decreasing intestinal absorption of glucose. (From Martindale, The Extra Pharmacopoeia, 30th ed, p289)</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>An agent belonging to the biguanide class of antidiabetics with antihyperglycemic activity. Metformin is associated with a very low incidence of lactic acidosis. This agent helps reduce LDL cholesterol and triglyceride levels, and is not associated with weight gain, and prevents the cardiovascular complications of diabetes. Metformin is not metabolized and is excreted unchanged by the kidneys.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Dimethylbiguanidine
Dimethylbiguanid
Metforminum
Metformin
Metformin (substance)
Metformin-containing product
Imidodicarbonimidic diamide NN-dimethyl-
NN-dimethylbiguanide
11-Dimethylbiguanide
Product containing metformin (medicinal product)
Dimethylguanylguanidine
Metformine
NN-Dimethylimidodicarbonimidic Diamide
Metformina
HCl Metformin
Metformin HCl
Hydrochloride Metformin
Glucophage
Metformin Hydrochloride</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Metformin</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


