    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass675ee9d3_f2e7_42b9_8b5b_b267b1446672 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass675ee9d3_f2e7_42b9_8b5b_b267b1446672">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass39a4d378_0f9d_4575_a075_6eea22aefc9c"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>胃旁路术</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>Surgical procedure in which the STOMACH is transected high on the body. The resulting small proximal gastric pouch is joined to any parts of the SMALL INTESTINE by an end-to-side SURGICAL ANASTOMOSIS, depending on the amounts of intestinal surface being bypasses. This procedure is used frequently in the treatment of MORBID OBESITY by limiting the size of functional STOMACH, food intake, and food absorption.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Gastric bypass NOS
Bypass of stomach
stomach bypass
Gastric bypass
Bypass of stomach (procedure)
Bypass Gastric</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Gastric bypass</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass67816dba_8493_4720_804d_7e1ca0a2a2c0 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass67816dba_8493_4720_804d_7e1ca0a2a2c0">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassb57a8d58_f930_4e0f_a3c5_cdfddadd4c4d"/>
        <OWLAnnotationProperty3edd358c_ddd9_4ca1_b651_9cf80cd296b0>计划妊娠：对癫痫有效控制且可能减停药物的女性癫痫患者，建议在停用AEDs 6个月后可考虑计划妊娠。如果癫痫患者不可能停用药物而计划怀孕，癫痫专科医师应尽量将AEDs调整至单药治疗的低剂量，再建议患者怀孕，并告知如下风险：癫痫发作本身及AEDs均对胎儿有负面影响。如丙戊酸800 mg以上的13剂量可增加胎儿致畸的风险。推荐癫痫女性孕前3个月每天服用叶酸≤5 mg，以减少叶酸代谢相关致胎儿畸形的风险。
&quot;关于成人癫痫患者长程管理的专家共识.&quot; 中华神经科杂志 .07(2013):496-499.

应与产科医生密切合作，共同随访和监护女性癫痫孕产妇。管理的主要目标是尽量减少孕期癫痫发作和AEDs对胎儿的影响。
&quot;关于成人癫痫患者长程管理的专家共识.&quot; 中华神经科杂志 .07(2013):496-499.

建议患者在分娩前做好哺乳及照顾婴儿的准备，分娩后需及时调整AEDs剂量，尤其是妊娠中AEDs剂量较大的患者，产后AEDs的浓度上升，调整不及时将可能会导致药物中毒。
&quot;关于成人癫痫患者长程管理的专家共识.&quot; 中华神经科杂志 .07(2013):496-499.

妊娠期生理变化可影响AEDs的代谢。因此，妊娠期需定期监测AEDs血药浓度，并结合临床发作情况及药物不良反应调整AEDs剂量，尽量控制癫痫发作。
&quot;关于成人癫痫患者长程管理的专家共识.&quot; 中华神经科杂志 .07(2013):496-499.

AEDs的致畸性：在能够控制癫痫发作的情况下，尽可能避免多药治疗。在单药治疗的患者中尽可能降低药物剂量。常用AEDs中以丙戊酸和苯巴比妥的致畸率最高，应尽量避免在妊娠期妇女中使用。如果因为病情需要而必须选择丙戊酸治疗，应当使用800 mg以下日剂量的单药治疗。有证据表明，新型AEDs如拉莫三嗪等致畸率较低。其他新型AEDs尚无大规模妊娠登记。
&quot;关于成人癫痫患者长程管理的专家共识.&quot; 中华神经科杂志 .07(2013):496-499.</OWLAnnotationProperty3edd358c_ddd9_4ca1_b651_9cf80cd296b0>
        <OWLAnnotationProperty5b4bece4_34a5_4955_86ae_fe5305e84ce9>脑电图和血药浓度有助于对患者进行管理。VPA血药浓度可以作为指导，但其个体差异很大，缺乏关于母体血药浓度与MCMs风险之间的关系的证据。建议将VPA水平根据临床反应维持在推荐治疗范围以下。脑电图并不是可靠的指标。
Patient management will vary across diferent national health systems. EEG recordings and plasma drug concentration measurements, for example, may be part of national epilepsy management guidelines. Plasma valproate levels may be used as a guide, but interindividual doses vary widely and defnitive data on the association between maternal plasma drug levels and MCM risks are lacking. The target valproate level can be maintained below the recommended therapeutic range, depending on clinical response. EEG recordings are not a reliable biomarker of clinical response, but they can be of help when interpreted by an epilepsy specialist. Family planning is important in patients taking AEDs. 
Toledo M, Mostacci B, Bosak M, Jedrzejzak J, Thomas RH, Salas-Puig J, Biraben A, Schmitz B. Expert opinion: use of valproate in girls and women of childbearing potential with epilepsy: recommendations and alternatives based on a review of the literature and clinical experience-a European perspective. J Neurol. 2020 Apr 1. doi: 10.1007/s00415-020-09809-0. Epub ahead of print. PMID: 32239268.

Unplanned pregnancies in women with epilepsy on valproate
专家小组建议在计划外妊娠的任何阶段（妊娠早、中、晚期）都应对VPA的使用和剂量进行重新评估（见下表）。在服用VPA期间，妊娠WWE应尽可能考虑使用最低有效剂量VPA。妊娠早期尽量停药或减少剂量，以避免后代认知障碍。如果决定换药，左乙拉西坦比拉莫三嗪更可取。对于GTCS复发风险较高的孕妇，VPA的剂量必须保持稳定。
在服用VPA的患者发生计划外怀孕时，应对癫痫史、癫痫发作风险、致畸风险和患者偏好等因素进行评估，向患者提供MCMs的信息和相关咨询，协助她们做出最佳的决定。同时应密切监测妊娠（如，使用高分辨超声）。
Although precise data are lacking, the expert panel considers that valproate use and dosage should be reassessed at any stage of an unplanned pregnancy (first, second, or third trimester) (Table 3). As a general recommendation, a woman who becomes pregnant while on valproate should be switched to as low a dose as possible for as long as possible. The priority in the first trimester should probably be to withdraw the drug or reduce the dose to prevent cognitive impairment in the newborn. If a switch is decided, levetiracetam is preferable to lamotrigine, as it can be quickly loaded, either orally or intravenously. Valproate doses must be kept stable in pregnant women at high risk of GTCS recurrence.
The following factors should all be considered in the event of an unplanned pregnancy in a patient on valproate: epilepsy history, seizure risk, teratogenic risk, and patient preferences (Table 3). The pregnancy should be closely monitored (e.g., with high-resolution ultrasound). The consequences of any MCM detected should be discussed in depth and women should be offered counselling to help them take the best possible decision regarding pregnancy termination in accordance with local laws.
Toledo M, Mostacci B, Bosak M, Jedrzejzak J, Thomas RH, Salas-Puig J, Biraben A, Schmitz B. Expert opinion: use of valproate in girls and women of childbearing potential with epilepsy: recommendations and alternatives based on a review of the literature and clinical experience-a European perspective. J Neurol. 2020 Apr 1. doi: 10.1007/s00415-020-09809-0. Epub ahead of print. PMID: 32239268.</OWLAnnotationProperty5b4bece4_34a5_4955_86ae_fe5305e84ce9>
        <OWLAnnotationProperty70d24189_e686_401a_bf66_f45f9e22e333>如需换药，应当保证在妊娠前达到有效的血药浓度。
中国医师协会神经内科分会癫(癎)专委会. &quot;妊娠期女性抗癫(癎)药物应用中国专家共识.&quot; 中国医师杂志 17.7(2015):969-971.

建议：(1)所有AEDs调整最好在受孕前完成；(2)尽量在癫痫发作控制稳定后开始备孕，尤其是对于全身强直阵-挛性发作患者；(3)尽可能避免使用丙戊酸、扑痢酮、苯巴比妥等；(4)尽量将AEDs调整至单药治疗的最低有效剂量。
中国医师协会神经内科分会癫(癎)专委会. &quot;妊娠期女性抗癫(癎)药物应用中国专家共识.&quot; 中国医师杂志 17.7(2015):969-971.

妊娠期间癫痫发作会对母体和胎儿产生不良影响，因此妊娠期女性患者除了常规的产前检查，还应定期就诊癫痫专科。根据临床表现和脑电图等检查，动态评估患者是否仍有癫痫发作并明确发作类型，以便及时调整药物剂量和种类。
中国医师协会神经内科分会癫(癎)专委会. &quot;妊娠期女性抗癫(癎)药物应用中国专家共识.&quot; 中国医师杂志 17.7(2015):969-971.

妊娠期间应尽可能避免多药联合治疗。
中国医师协会神经内科分会癫(癎)专委会. &quot;妊娠期女性抗癫(癎)药物应用中国专家共识.&quot; 中国医师杂志 17.7(2015):969-971.

女性癫痫患者在产后仍应继续服用AEDs。
通常建议在产后数周内，逐渐减量至妊娠前水平
中国医师协会神经内科分会癫(癎)专委会. &quot;妊娠期女性抗癫(癎)药物应用中国专家共识.&quot; 中国医师杂志 17.7(2015):969-971.

建议患者产前每两个月行一次血药浓度监测，如出现控制不佳，应及时调整AEDs剂量。中国医师协会神经内科分会癫(癎)专委会. &quot;妊娠期女性抗癫(癎)药物应用中国专家共识.&quot; 中国医师杂志 17.7(2015):969-971.

在整个围产期，患者应当规律服用AEDs，同时注意避免睡眠、情绪等因素的影响。
中国医师协会神经内科分会癫(癎)专委会. &quot;妊娠期女性抗癫(癎)药物应用中国专家共识.&quot; 中国医师杂志 17.7(2015):969-971.</OWLAnnotationProperty70d24189_e686_401a_bf66_f45f9e22e333>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>抗癫痫药物调整</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>Change of type，number or dose of antiseizure medications</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NICE_guidance>The clinician should discuss with the woman and girl the relative benefits and risks of adjusting medication to enable her to make an informed decision. Where appropriate, the woman or girl&apos;s specialist should be consulted. [2004]
临床医生应与妇女和女孩讨论调整药物的相对益处和风险，以使她能够做出明智的决定。在适当的情况下，应咨询该女性的专科医生。
nice.org.uk/guidance/cg137</untitled-ontology-34:NICE_guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:ROCG_Guidance>[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:B] The lowest effective dose of the most appropriate AED should be used.
【推荐等级：B】妊娠期WWE应选用适宜的最低有效剂量的AEDs。
Exposure to sodium valproate and other AED polytherapy should be minimised by changing the medication prior to conception, as recommended by an epilepsy specialist after a careful evaluation of the potential risks and benefits.
孕前使用VPA和其他AEDs综合治疗的患者，应根据癫痫专家的评估和建议下，在孕前即更换药物，以最大限度减少风险。
https://www.rcog.org.uk/guidance/browse-all-guidance/green-top-guidelines/epilepsy-in-pregnancy-green-top-guideline-no-68/</untitled-ontology-34:ROCG_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>For women with epilepsy who require treatment with antiepileptic drugs during pregnancy the relative risks of seizures and risks of fetal, neonatal and childhood problems should be discussed.C  onsideration may be given to withdrawal of antiepileptic drugs prior to conception if circumstances are favourable. The decision should only be made if the epilepsy is in remission, the risk of recurrent seizures is low and the woman is aware of the consequences of recurrent seizures.Wherever possible, a woman should conceive on the lowest effective dose of one AED appropriate for her epilepsy syndrome. If she has good seizure control and presents already pregnant, there is probably little to be gained by altering her AEDs
对于需要在妊娠期间使用AEDs的女性癫痫患者，应权衡癫痫发作的风险和对后代的风险。如果条件允许（癫痫缓解、复发风险很低并且患者充分了解后果），可以考虑在怀孕前停用AEDs。如果需要在妊娠期使用AEDs，应以最低有效剂量进行治疗。妊娠期间尽量不要改变患者AEDs种类。
Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network.Diagnosis and management of epilepsy in adults. SIGN 143. Edinburgh, SIGN, 2015. Available at: www.sign.ac.uk/guidelines/fulltext/143/index.html</untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>Given the morbidity and mortality risks associated with seizures (including sudden unexpected death in epilepsy) no antiepileptic drug should be discontinued during pregnancy unless this has been discussed with an epilepsy specialist.
考虑到与癫痫发作相关的发病率和死亡率（包括SUDEP），妊娠期不应停止使用任何AEDs。
Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network.Diagnosis and management of epilepsy in adults. SIGN 143. Edinburgh, SIGN, 2015. Available at: www.sign.ac.uk/guidelines/fulltext/143/index.html</untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>If seizure control deteriorates during pregnancy, other factors affecting AED levels in pregnancy should be considered (for example vomiting, interactions with other medication).
如果妊娠期癫痫控制不良，应考虑任何在妊娠期可影响AEDs药物浓度的因素，如呕吐、药物相互作用等。
Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network.Diagnosis and management of epilepsy in adults. SIGN 143. Edinburgh, SIGN, 2015. Available at: www.sign.ac.uk/guidelines/fulltext/143/index.html</untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:C] Women with epilepsy should be reassured that antiepileptic drugs do not increase the risk of spontaneous miscarriage and stillbirth
C级推荐：应告知女性癫痫患者，AEDs不会增加自然流产和死产的风险。
Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network.Diagnosis and management of epilepsy in adults. SIGN 143. Edinburgh, SIGN, 2015. Available at: www.sign.ac.uk/guidelines/fulltext/143/index.html</untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:D]In pregnancy, dosing adjustment for the majority of antiepileptic drugs (with the exception of lamotrigine and levetiracetam) should only be considered if there is a change in seizure frequency or if toxicity is suspected.
D级推荐：在妊娠期，只有在癫痫发作频率变化或怀疑有药物中毒可能的时候才考虑调整AEDs的剂量（除LTG和LEV外）。
Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network.Diagnosis and management of epilepsy in adults. SIGN 143. Edinburgh, SIGN, 2015. Available at: www.sign.ac.uk/guidelines/fulltext/143/index.html</untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Change of antiseizure medications</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Adjustment of antiseizure medications</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass67bd0156_7994_4701_b260_30be28b0486a -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass67bd0156_7994_4701_b260_30be28b0486a">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass1d1e8181_8310_4160_9b14_2fdfec047a82"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>免疫</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>Protected against infectious disease by either specific or non-specific mechanisms.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Immune (qualifier value)
Immune</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Immune</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass685fcc84_37dc_4b54_b895_5a492b653878 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass685fcc84_37dc_4b54_b895_5a492b653878">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassdb042738_d57a_46c1_ad80_e6b53c4c5d2a"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>肾上腺素能β拮抗剂</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>Drugs that bind to and block the activation of ADRENERGIC BETA-2 RECEPTORS.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Beta-2 adrenergic receptor blocker
beta2-Adrenergic Antagonists
Adrenergic beta2-Antagonists
Adrenergic beta 2 Receptor Antagonists
Adrenergic beta2 Antagonists
