    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass6dcca81f_66a5_452c_82d0_ed678543752d">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassc8e9bc0b_9b47_4b42_9657_742013ac8411"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>癫痫发作类型</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>Classification of seizure type take into account the results of investigations such as electroencephalography (EEG) and neuroimaging studies together with other studies exploring the underlying etiology of the epilepsy.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:D] Women should be aware that their seizure pattern may change around the menopause.
D级推荐：女性癫痫患者的痫发作模式可能在更年期前后发生变化。
Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network.Diagnosis and management of epilepsy in adults. SIGN 143. Edinburgh, SIGN, 2015. Available at: www.sign.ac.uk/guidelines/fulltext/143/index.html</untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>GEFS+2
GEFSP2
GENERALIZED EPILEPSY WITH FEBRILE SEIZURES PLUS TYPE 2
Generalized Epilepsy With Febrile Seizures Plus Type 2
GEFS Type 2
GEFS+ TYPE 2</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Seizure types</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Seizure type</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


