    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass703138e7_a7b3_4480_a014_6c9563f77a10 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass703138e7_a7b3_4480_a014_6c9563f77a10">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass50b2e20a_e0c9_49a7_b253_ff13742cb19d"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>利物浦癫痫严重程度量表</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>The Liverpool Seizure Severity Scale (LSSS) is a valid and reliable test for quantifying seizure severity that may also be used to detect changes in seizure severity over time. The Liverpool Seizure Severity Scale is composed of 12 items and is scored on a Likert scale. Previously, the use of the LSSS in clinical trials yielded promising data. In addition, a modification has been made to the LSSS as well as the scoring system to make it more clinically reliable and user-friendly. The validity, reliability, and responsiveness of the revised LSSS also have been demonstrated(备注：参考PMID: 24440688)</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Liverpool seizure severity scale</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass7037a3a0_ff17_4990_9298_d71601d44523 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass7037a3a0_ff17_4990_9298_d71601d44523">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass66ab68e0_1089_40c9_8b6a_99ddbf3b157a"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>抗癫痫药物调整</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>Change of type，number or dose of antiseizure medications</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Change of antiseizure medications</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Adjustment of antiseizure medications</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass70e4e311_e8e4_4f77_bcc4_3544934aab5f -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass70e4e311_e8e4_4f77_bcc4_3544934aab5f">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassc27bf42d_b77e_460f_8c7f_45ba0580f229"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>认知行为治疗</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>A directive form of psychotherapy based on the interpretation of situations (cognitive structure of experiences) that determine how an individual feels and behaves. It is based on the premise that cognition, the process of acquiring knowledge and forming beliefs, is a primary determinant of mood and behavior. The therapy uses behavioral and verbal techniques to identify and correct negative thinking that is at the root of the aberrant behavior.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>A type of psychotherapy utilized to treat different forms of mental disorders.The treatment involves the identification of unhelpful or destructive patterns of thinking and behaviors and the subsequent replacement with behaviors that are beneficial and constructive.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
