        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>单胺氧化酶抑制剂</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>A chemically heterogeneous group of drugs that have in common the ability to block oxidative deamination of naturally occurring monoamines. (From Gilman, et al., Goodman and Gilman&apos;s The Pharmacological Basis of Therapeutics, 8th ed, p414)</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>Any substance that inhibits monoamine oxidase (MAO), an enzyme that catalyzes the oxidative deamination of monoamines and plays a role in the inactivation of neurotransmitters.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
