    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass8268657e_5964_424f_8bdd_21e2a9b84677 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass8268657e_5964_424f_8bdd_21e2a9b84677">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassdd746922_f5f4_45b7_9f02_91092fa08d45"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>钠-葡萄糖协同转运蛋白2抑制剂</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>Sodium-dependent glucose transporter (SGLT) 2 is specifically expressed in the kidney, while SGLT1 is present in the kidneys and small intestine. SGLT2 inhibitors are a class of oral antidiabetic drugs that lower elevated plasma glucose levels by promoting the urinary excretion of excess glucose through the inhibition of renal glucose reuptake</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>SGLT2</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Sodium-dependent glucose transporters 2 inhibitor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass82a8342d_66da_44e3_9e3b_fdda0b38f155 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass82a8342d_66da_44e3_9e3b_fdda0b38f155">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9abdfeac_655b_41c6_bb76_7a99b7ca8dea"/>
        <OWLAnnotationPropertyd448a312_221a_4215_b2b2_684d470bc1f8>WWE在生育和性行为方面主要面临着更高的不孕不育率和性功能障碍率。
Higher rates of infertility and sexual dysfunction.
Mauri Llerda JA, Suller Marti A, de la Peña Mayor P, Martínez Ferri M, Poza Aldea JJ, Gomez Alonso J, Mercadé Cerdá JM. The Spanish Society of Neurology&apos;s official clinical practice guidelines for epilepsy. Special considerations in epilepsy: comorbidities, women of childbearing age, and elderly patients. Neurologia. 2015 Oct;30(8):510-7. English, Spanish. doi: 10.1016/j.nrl.2014.08.002. Epub 2015 Jan 21. PMID: 25618222.</OWLAnnotationPropertyd448a312_221a_4215_b2b2_684d470bc1f8>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>性功能障碍</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>Disturbances in sexual desire or performance.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>sexual dysfunction
Sexual function abnormal
Sexual dysfunction NOS
Sexual Dysfunction
SEXUAL DYSFUNCTION
Abnormal sexual function
Abnormal sexual function (finding)
Sexual dysfunction unspecified</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Sexual dysfunction</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass82d4102c_4088_4a26_a5d8_028c5f4be70c -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass82d4102c_4088_4a26_a5d8_028c5f4be70c">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassea7ed860_0005_4dc3_9a2f_724164a2d9e8"/>
        <OWLAnnotationProperty5b4bece4_34a5_4955_86ae_fe5305e84ce9>WOCP指处于月经初潮和更年期之间的女性，这些女性具有生育能力。专家小组认为，丙戊酸不应作为WOCP的一线治疗。
不推荐在月经初潮前开始服用丙戊酸，但在某些特殊情况下可以接受（如：丙戊酸盐可以最为潜在的自限性癫痫综合征的一线治疗药物，包括伴有中央颞部棘波的局灶性癫痫、儿童期失神发作、婴儿良性肌阵挛癫痫）。对于慢性的儿童期发作、可能持续到青春期和成年期的癫痫综合征患者而言（如，Jeavons综合症），丙戊酸不应作为首选治疗。总的来说，专家小组不建议将丙戊酸作为10岁以上女性任何类型癫痫的一线治疗。
The panel considered that there are no clinical situations in which valproate should be started as first-line therapy in WOCP.Initiation of valproate before menarche is not recommended, although there are circumstances when it might be acceptable. Valproate can be prescribed as first-line therapy for potentially self-limited epilepsy syndromes, such as focal epilepsy with centrotemporal spikes, childhood absence epilepsy, and benign myoclonic epilepsy in infancy. It should not be the first choice in patients with chronic childhood-onset epilepsy syndromes likely to remain active into adolescence and adulthood (e.g., Jeavons syndrome). Overall, the panel does not recommend starting valproate as first-line treatment for epilepsy of any type in girls older than 10 years.
Toledo M, Mostacci B, Bosak M, Jedrzejzak J, Thomas RH, Salas-Puig J, Biraben A, Schmitz B. Expert opinion: use of valproate in girls and women of childbearing potential with epilepsy: recommendations and alternatives based on a review of the literature and clinical experience-a European perspective. J Neurol. 2020 Apr 1. doi: 10.1007/s00415-020-09809-0. Epub ahead of print. PMID: 32239268.</OWLAnnotationProperty5b4bece4_34a5_4955_86ae_fe5305e84ce9>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>良性婴儿肌阵挛性癫痫</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Benign myoclonic epilepsy in infancy
Benign Infantile Myoclonic Epilepsy
Myoclonic Epilepsy Benign Infantile
Epilepsy Myoclonic Infantile Benign
Myoclonic Epilepsy Infantile Benign
Benign myoclonic epilepsy in infancy (disorder)
Neonatal myoclonic epilepsy</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Benign myoclonic epilepsy in infancy</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass82efdf2f_8dfe_485b_9ae8_83fa1348e699 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass82efdf2f_8dfe_485b_9ae8_83fa1348e699">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassdd746922_f5f4_45b7_9f02_91092fa08d45"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>安非他酮</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>A propiophenone-derived antidepressant and antismoking agent that inhibits the uptake of DOPAMINE.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>An aminoketone with antidepressant activity. The molecular mechanism of the antidepressant effect of bupropion is unknown. This agent does not inhibit monoamine oxidase and, compared to classical tricyclic antidepressants, is a weak blocker of the neuronal uptake of serotonin and norepinephrine. Buproprion also weakly inhibits the neuronal re-uptake of dopamine.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Amfebutamone
1-Propanone 1-(3-Chlorophenyl)-2-((11-dimethylethyl)amino)-
BUPROPION
(+-)-1-(3-Chlorophenyl)-2-((11-dimethylethyl)amino)-1-propanone
Amfebutamon
Bupropion-containing product
Bupropion (substance)
Product containing bupropion (medicinal product)</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Bupropion</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass859cb2a7_1127_49bf_9166_59a646a89745 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass859cb2a7_1127_49bf_9166_59a646a89745">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9e8550e9_9259_4826_a257_3569677963b0"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>苯妥英钠</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>An anticonvulsant that is used to treat a wide variety of seizures. It is also an anti-arrhythmic and a muscle relaxant. The mechanism of therapeutic action is not clear, although several cellular actions have been described including effects on ion channels, active transport, and general membrane stabilization. The mechanism of its muscle relaxant effect appears to involve a reduction in the sensitivity of muscle spindles to stretch. Phenytoin has been proposed for several other therapeutic uses, but its use has been limited by its many adverse effects and interactions with other drugs.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>The sodium salt form of phenytoin, a hydantoin derivate and non-sedative antiepileptic agent with anticonvulsant activity. Phenytoin sodium promotes sodium efflux from neurons located in the motor cortex, thereby stabilizing the neuron and inhibiting synaptic transmission. This leads to a reduction in posttetanic potentiation at synapses, an inhibition of repetitive firing of action potentials and ultimately inhibits the spread of seizure activity.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:ROCG_Guidance>[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:C] Based on limited evidence, in utero exposure to carbamazepine and lamotrigine does not appear to adversely affect neurodevelopment of the offspring. There is very little evidence for levetiracetam and phenytoin. Parents should be informed that evidence on long-term outcomes is based on small numbers of children.
【推荐等级：C】应告知WWE及其伴侣，关于宫内暴露于AEDs产生的长期神经发育结果是基于少数儿童的。有限的证据表示，宫内接触CBZ和LTG似乎不会影响后代神经生长发育；使用LEV和PHT的证据很少。
https://www.rcog.org.uk/guidance/browse-all-guidance/green-top-guidelines/epilepsy-in-pregnancy-green-top-guideline-no-68/</untitled-ontology-34:ROCG_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:ROCG_Guidance>[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:C] Women taking enzyme-inducing AEDs (carbamazepine, phenytoin, phenobarbital, primidone, oxcarbazepine, topiramate and eslicarbazepine) should be counselled about the risk of failure with some hormonal contraceptives.
【推荐等级：C】应告知服用酶诱导型AEDs（卡马西平、苯妥英、苯巴比妥、扑米酮、奥卡西平、托吡酯、艾司利卡西平）的WWE避孕失败的风险。
https://www.rcog.org.uk/guidance/browse-all-guidance/green-top-guidelines/epilepsy-in-pregnancy-green-top-guideline-no-68/</untitled-ontology-34:ROCG_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>55-Diphenyl-24-imidazolidinedione Monosodium Salt
phenytoin sodium
Diphenylhydantoin sodium
Diphenylhydantoinate Sodium
Phenytoin sodium (substance)
