        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>Inflammation of the COLON that is predominantly confined to the MUCOSA. Its major symptoms include DIARRHEA, rectal BLEEDING, the passage of MUCUS, and ABDOMINAL PAIN.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>An inflammatory bowel disease involving the mucosal surface of the large intestine and rectum. It may present with an acute or slow onset and follows an intermittent or continuous course. Signs and symptoms include abdominal pain, diarrhea, fever, weight loss, and intestinal hemorrhage.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
