    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass962129a8_2b55_4d19_b63d_1c1da3c466dc -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass962129a8_2b55_4d19_b63d_1c1da3c466dc">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassea7ed860_0005_4dc3_9a2f_724164a2d9e8"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>Rasmussen综合征</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>Inflammation of the BRAIN due to infection, autoimmune processes, toxins, and other conditions. Viral infections (see ENCEPHALITIS, VIRAL) are a relatively frequent cause of this condition.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Brain Inflammation
Inflammation Brain
Brain Inflammations
Rasmussen Syndrome
Rasmussen Encephalitis
Rasmussens Syndrome
Encephalitis Rasmussen</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Rasmussen syndroms</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass96b88d5e_fdb3_4d6d_967c_158948a8e9eb -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass96b88d5e_fdb3_4d6d_967c_158948a8e9eb">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassdd746922_f5f4_45b7_9f02_91092fa08d45"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>芬特明</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>A central nervous system stimulant and sympathomimetic with actions and uses similar to those of DEXTROAMPHETAMINE. It has been used most frequently in the treatment of obesity.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>A natural monoamine alkaloid derivative and a sympathomimetic stimulant with appetite suppressant property. Phentermine, which was part of the Fen-Phen anti-obesity medication, stimulates hypothalamic release of norepinephrine, a neurotransmitter involved in stress responses (fight-or-flight reactions), and reduces hunger sensation. Phentermine also causes the release of epinephrine or adrenaline outside of the brain, resulting in breakdown of stored fat.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Phenyl-tertiary-butylamine
11-Dimethyl-2-phenylethylamine
Phentermine
Fentermina
Benzeneethanamine alphaalpha-dimethyl-
Product containing phentermine (medicinal product)
Phentermine-containing product
2-Amino-2-methyl-1-phenylpropane
Phentermine (substance)
2-Phenyl-tert-butylamine
alphaalpha-Dimethylphenethylamine
Phenterminum</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Phentermine</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass96e7e0f0_df16_4982_905d_ad2dc9084b39 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass96e7e0f0_df16_4982_905d_ad2dc9084b39">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9abdfeac_655b_41c6_bb76_7a99b7ca8dea"/>
        <OWLAnnotationPropertyd448a312_221a_4215_b2b2_684d470bc1f8>WWE同样也有更高的多囊卵巢综合征患病率，即使是在没有服用AEDs的WWE中也是如此；在接受VPA治疗的WWE中，多囊卵巢综合征的患病率会增加，尤其是在20岁之前即开始接受治疗的患者中。
A higher prevalence of polycystic ovary syndrome, even in women not taking AEDs. This prevalence increases in patients treated with VPA, especially when treatment onset is before the age of 20.
Mauri Llerda JA, Suller Marti A, de la Peña Mayor P, Martínez Ferri M, Poza Aldea JJ, Gomez Alonso J, Mercadé Cerdá JM. The Spanish Society of Neurology&apos;s official clinical practice guidelines for epilepsy. Special considerations in epilepsy: comorbidities, women of childbearing age, and elderly patients. Neurologia. 2015 Oct;30(8):510-7. English, Spanish. doi: 10.1016/j.nrl.2014.08.002. Epub 2015 Jan 21. PMID: 25618222.</OWLAnnotationPropertyd448a312_221a_4215_b2b2_684d470bc1f8>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>多囊卵巢综合征</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>A complex disorder characterized by infertility, HIRSUTISM; OBESITY; and various menstrual disturbances such as OLIGOMENORRHEA; AMENORRHEA; ANOVULATION. Polycystic ovary syndrome is usually associated with bilateral enlarged ovaries studded with atretic follicles, not with cysts. The term, polycystic ovary, is misleading.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>A disorder that manifests as multiple cysts on the ovaries. It results in hormonal imbalances and leads to irregular and abnormal menstrual periods, excess growth of hair, acne eruptions and obesity.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>polycystic ovary disorder
Polycystic ovary disease
Stein-Leventhal Syndrome
Stein Leventhal Syndrome
PCO1
