    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass99f3dd2f_b26d_4a12_a593_a163a8882a8a -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass99f3dd2f_b26d_4a12_a593_a163a8882a8a">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org//Childbearing-ageWomenwithEpilepsyOntology#OWLClass0db655e6_fcdc_45ba_a5c9_4508ac0dd74b"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>长效避孕针</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>Injectable contraceptives are used to prevent conception along with convenience, privacy, safe and efficient protection to women. Depo medroxy progesterone acetate (DMPA) is currently used by reproductive women of 130 countries</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NICE_guidance>The use of additional barrier methods should be discussed with women and girls taking enzyme-inducing AEDs and oral contraception or having depot injections of progestogen[23].[2004, amended 2012]
应将额外的外用避孕方法的用途告知与服用酶诱导型抗癫痫药和口服避孕药或长期注射孕激素的女性[23]。[2004 年，2012 年修订]
nice.org.uk/guidance/cg137</untitled-ontology-34:NICE_guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>injectable contraceptive</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Contraception injection</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9a12dad9_5bb9_41cc_8673_21bf0288c0c0 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9a12dad9_5bb9_41cc_8673_21bf0288c0c0">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassb5313e9d_0836_44f6_ae6b_224bf17a6349"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>匹莫齐特</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>A diphenylbutylpiperidine that is effective as an antipsychotic agent and as an alternative to HALOPERIDOL for the suppression of vocal and motor tics in patients with Tourette syndrome. Although the precise mechanism of action is unknown, blockade of postsynaptic dopamine receptors has been postulated. (From AMA Drug Evaluations Annual, 1994, p403)</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>A diphenylbutylpiperidine derivative and a dopamine antagonist with antipsychotic property. Pimozide selectively inhibits type 2 dopaminergic receptors in the central nervous system (CNS), thereby decreasing dopamine neurotransmission and reducing the occurrence of motor and vocal tics and delusions of parasitosis. In addition, this agent antagonizes alpha-adrenergic and 5-HT2 receptors.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Product containing pimozide (medicinal product)
Pimozida
2H-Benzimidazol-2-one 1-(1-(44-bis(4-fluorophenyl)butyl)-4-piperidinyl)-13-dihydro-
Orap
Pimozidum
Pimozide
Pimozide-containing product
Orap forte
Opiran
Pimozide (substance)</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Pimozide</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9a587443_7cc8_4915_a6bb_b7813fba79b7 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9a587443_7cc8_4915_a6bb_b7813fba79b7">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassdd746922_f5f4_45b7_9f02_91092fa08d45"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>纳曲酮</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>Derivative of noroxymorphone that is the N-cyclopropylmethyl congener of NALOXONE. It is a narcotic antagonist that is effective orally, longer lasting and more potent than naloxone, and has been proposed for the treatment of heroin addiction. The FDA has approved naltrexone for the treatment of alcohol dependence.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>A noroxymorphone derivative with competitive opioid antagonistic property. Naltrexone reverses the effects of opioid analgesics by binding to the various opioid receptors in the central nervous system, including the mu-, kappa- and gamma-opioid receptors. This leads to an inhibition of the typical actions of opioid analgesics, including analgesia, euphoria, sedation, respiratory depression, miosis, bradycardia, and physical dependence. Naltrexone is longer-acting and more potent compared to naloxone.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Naltrexone-containing product
vivitrol
17-(Cyclopropylmethyl)-45α-epoxy-314-dihydroxymorphinan-6-one
Naltrexone
Morphinan-6-one 17-(cyclopropylmethyl)-45-epoxy-314-dihydroxy- (5alpha)-
Naltrexon
N-Cyclopropylmethylnoroxymorphone
Naltrexonum
17-(Cyclopropylmethyl)-45-epoxy-314-dihydroxymorphinan-6-one
Naltrexone (substance)
N-Cyclopropylmethyl-14-hydroxydihydromorphinone
Naltrexona
Product containing naltrexone (medicinal product)</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Naltrexone</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


