    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9f72fbd8_62d8_48ff_9e14_1b1ec34cda0c -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9f72fbd8_62d8_48ff_9e14_1b1ec34cda0c">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org//Childbearing-ageWomenwithEpilepsyOntology#OWLClassde18b6e3_5aab_4eba_937e_3c256c84cdb6"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>共患病诊断</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>The presence of co-existing or additional diseases with reference to an initial diagnosis or with reference to the index condition that is the subject of study. Comorbidity may affect the ability of affected individuals to function and also their survival; it may be used as a prognostic indicator for length of hospital stay, cost factors, and outcome or survival.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>A diagnosis is an assertion that a patient has comorbidities</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>comorbidities diagnosis
co-morbidity
comorbidities
comorbidity
Intercurrent illness</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Comorbidities</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9f82d948_7acb_4c97_a843_d359d5a000c5 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9f82d948_7acb_4c97_a843_d359d5a000c5">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassdd746922_f5f4_45b7_9f02_91092fa08d45"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>α-糖苷酶抑制剂</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>Alpha-glycosidase inhibitor (AGIs) inhibit the enzyme α-glucosidase at the brush border of the intestinal epithelium, thus blocking the absorption of carbohydrates in the small intestine. They are administered with the first bite of a carbohydrate-containing meal and limit postprandial hyperglycemia without causing hypoglycemia. Their use has been limited by frequent GI complaints, the need to administer the drugs at the beginning of each meal, only modest reduction in HbA1c levels, and limited effect on fasting glucose levels</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>AGIs</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Alpha-glycosidase inhibitor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9fcd783c_67ec_4c75_8dbe_24c463dbf031 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9fcd783c_67ec_4c75_8dbe_24c463dbf031">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass8b6a43a9_4b05_4045_abdb_d54b2493a79b"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>激素避孕</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>Contraceptive methods that utilize HORMONAL CONTRACEPTIVE AGENTS.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>The birth control method that utilizes external source of sex hormones to prevent pregnancy by interfering with the ovulation, fertilization or implantation of the fertilized egg in the uterus.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:ROCG_Guidance>[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:C] Women taking lamotrigine monotherapy and oestrogen-containing contraceptives should be informed of the potential increase in seizures due to a fall in the levels of lamotrigine.
【推荐等级：C】应告知同时服用拉莫三嗪（单一疗法）和含雌激素避孕药的WWE，由于拉莫三嗪水平的下降，癫痫发作的风险增加。
https://www.rcog.org.uk/guidance/browse-all-guidance/green-top-guidelines/epilepsy-in-pregnancy-green-top-guideline-no-68/</untitled-ontology-34:ROCG_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:C] To minimise the risk of contraceptive failure, a woman using any combined hormonal contraception, or a combined oral contraceptive pill, or a progesterone-only pill should be prescribed an antiepileptic drug that does not induce hepatic enzymes.
C级推荐：为避免将避孕失败的风险降到最低，使用联合避孕药、合用多种口服避孕药或仅服用黄体酮避孕药的妇女，应使用非肝酶诱导性AEDs。
Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network.Diagnosis and management of epilepsy in adults. SIGN 143. Edinburgh, SIGN, 2015. Available at: www.sign.ac.uk/guidelines/fulltext/143/index.html</untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>hormonal contraceptive type
hormonal_contraceptive_type
Hormonal Contraception
Contraception Hormonal
Hormonal contraception
Hormonal Birth Control</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Hormonal contraception</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassa154eb8d_990a_4e91_92c1_3b880d1d2434 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassa154eb8d_990a_4e91_92c1_3b880d1d2434">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass759708f9_95b8_4278_b245_68ead2726509"/>
        <OWLAnnotationProperty2b10dba6_b3e5_4601_aef4_e0f62595af79>哺乳：绝大多数AEDs可以通过乳汁分泌，但是乳汁中AEDs的浓度相对比较低；对于绝大多数服用AEDs的妇女来说，哺乳相对是安全的，应当鼓励母乳喂养；注意婴儿的不良反应，如易激惹、睡眠不良、体重减轻或镇静、肌张力降低、吸吮无力、进食困难等现象。
Li, S. and Hong, Z., 2015. Lin chuang zhen liao zhi nan. Beijing: Ren min wei sheng chu ban she.</OWLAnnotationProperty2b10dba6_b3e5_4601_aef4_e0f62595af79>
        <OWLAnnotationProperty2b10dba6_b3e5_4601_aef4_e0f62595af79>孕前咨询：告知患者癫痫发作及AEDs对妊娠及胎儿风险。妊娠期使用AEDs可能对癫痫女性后代智力发育造成影响，尤其是苯巴比妥和丙戊酸。目前尚无足够的证据来评估新型AEDs（加巴喷丁、左乙拉西坦、噻加宾、托吡酯、氨己烯酸）的致畸性。大剂量丙戊酸（超过800mg/天）以及联合丙戊酸的多药治疗的致畸风险明显增加；告知患者补充叶酸和维生素K的必要性。如果孕妇或者配偶有癫痫疾病，尤其是有特发性癫痫及癫痫及相关遗传病家族史者，应当进行遗传咨询。
Li, S. and Hong, Z., 2015. Lin chuang zhen liao zhi nan. Beijing: Ren min wei sheng chu ban she.</OWLAnnotationProperty2b10dba6_b3e5_4601_aef4_e0f62595af79>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>噻加宾</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>A nipecotic acid derivative that acts as a GABA uptake inhibitor and anticonvulsant agent. It is used in the treatment of EPILEPSY, for refractory PARTIAL SEIZURES.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Tiagabine Hydrochloride
Gabitril
NO 328
NO-328
NO 329
(R)-(44-bis(3-Methyl-2-thienyl)-3-butenyl)-3-piperidinecarboxylic acid Hydrochloride
Tiagabine (S)-isomer
NO-329
tiagabine
N-(44-di(3-Methylthien-2-yl)but-3-enyl)nipecotic acid
Tiagabine-containing product
Tiagabine (substance)
Tiagabina
Product containing tiagabine (medicinal product)
Tiagabinum
3-Piperidinecarboxylic acid 1-(44-bis(3-methyl-2-thienyl)-3-buten-1-yl)- (3R)-</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Tiagabine</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassa17b9d31_7c27_4d8b_8b57_77c5d871dc80 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassa17b9d31_7c27_4d8b_8b57_77c5d871dc80">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassc27bf42d_b77e_460f_8c7f_45ba0580f229"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>心理咨询</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>psychological counseling
Psychological counseling (procedure)
psychological counseling therapy
Psychological counselling</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Psychological counseling</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassa197488c_d576_4ccd_9dd0_964e4cadc9e1 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassa197488c_d576_4ccd_9dd0_964e4cadc9e1">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassf833bdb1_70d0_4183_b254_14d79cf0d040"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>抗生素</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>Substances produced by microorganisms that can inhibit or suppress the growth of other microorganisms.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>Substances naturally produced by microorganisms or their derivatives that selectively target microorganisms not humans. Antibiotics kill or inhibit the growth of microorganisms by targeting components of the microbial cell absent from human cells, including bacterial cell walls, cell membrane, and 30S or 50S ribosomal subunits. These substances are used in the treatment of bacterial and other microbial infections.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Antibiotic Drugs
antimicrobial
Antibiotic
Antibiotic Therapy
Antibiotic Agents
antibiotics
Antibiotic (product)
Antimicrobial Agent</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Antibiotic</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassa1ab025b_f9b5_4834_8e9f_37ea35c90eff -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassa1ab025b_f9b5_4834_8e9f_37ea35c90eff">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClasse95453e4_18f0_4c36_a41c_932332f720e4"/>
        <OWLAnnotationProperty2b10dba6_b3e5_4601_aef4_e0f62595af79>孕前咨询：告知患者癫痫发作及AEDs对妊娠及胎儿风险。妊娠期使用AEDs可能对癫痫女性后代智力发育造成影响，尤其是苯巴比妥和丙戊酸。目前尚无足够的证据来评估新型AEDs（加巴喷丁、左乙拉西坦、噻加宾、托吡酯、氨己烯酸）的致畸性。大剂量丙戊酸（超过800mg/天）以及联合丙戊酸的多药治疗的致畸风险明显增加；告知患者补充叶酸和维生素K的必要性。如果孕妇或者配偶有癫痫疾病，尤其是有特发性癫痫及癫痫及相关遗传病家族史者，应当进行遗传咨询。
Li, S. and Hong, Z., 2015. Lin chuang zhen liao zhi nan. Beijing: Ren min wei sheng chu ban she.</OWLAnnotationProperty2b10dba6_b3e5_4601_aef4_e0f62595af79>
        <OWLAnnotationProperty3a25c542_bdd7_46eb_b2e9_ad871281c141>Does preconceptional folic acid supplementation reduce the risk of birth defects in neonates of WWE taking AEDs？（孕前补充叶酸对于暴露于AEDs的新生儿是否可降低出生缺陷的风险？）
结论：补充叶酸可能会降低WWE后代MCMs的风险（两项Ⅲ类研究）。数据不足以证明补充叶酸在WWE中有效，但同时也没有证据证明其有害。
建议：孕前补充叶酸可降低MCMs风险（Level C）。建议孕前和妊娠期补充至少0.4mg/d叶酸。
Conclusion: The risk of MCMs in the offspring of WWE is possibly decreased by folic acid supplementation (two adequately sensitive Class III studies).
Recommendation: Preconceptional folic acid supplementation in WWE may be considered to reduce the risk of MCMs (Level C).
Harden CL, Pennell PB, Koppel BS, Hovinga CA, Gidal B, Meador KJ, Hopp J, Ting TY, Hauser WA, Thurman D, Kaplan PW, Robinson JN, French JA, Wiebe S, Wilner AN, Vazquez B, Holmes L, Krumholz A, Finnell R, Shafer PO, Le Guen C; American Academy of Neurology; American Epilepsy Society. Practice parameter update: management issues for women with epilepsy--focus on pregnancy (an evidence-based review): vitamin K, folic acid, blood levels, and breastfeeding: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee and Therapeutics and Technology Assessment Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology and American Epilepsy Society. Neurology. 2009 Jul 14;73(2):142-9. doi: 10.1212/WNL.0b013e3181a6b325. Epub 2009 Apr 27. PMID: 19398680; PMCID: PMC3475193.</OWLAnnotationProperty3a25c542_bdd7_46eb_b2e9_ad871281c141>
        <OWLAnnotationProperty5b4bece4_34a5_4955_86ae_fe5305e84ce9>叶酸对于神经管缺陷的保护作用仍存在争议，但建议不管是否使用VPA，在怀孕前至少1个月开始补充叶酸。对服用AEDs的患者，叶酸推荐剂量为4-5mg/d（此剂量高于低风险女性的推荐剂量）。需要注意的是，低剂量的叶酸可能与神经管缺陷有关，而过量的叶酸（＞10mg/d）可能是有毒的。
As a general recommendation, contraception should be maintained for 3 months after valproate discontinuation to ensure full clearance and allow time to adapt to the new AED. Although the protective effect of folic acid against neural tube defects is still under debate, folic acid supplementation is recommended for at least 1 month before conception, regardless of valproate treatment [31]. The recommended dose for patients taking AEDs is 4–5 mg/day, which is higher than doses recommended for women at low risk. It should be noted that low folic acid doses may be associated with neural tube defects and that excessive doses (&gt;10 mg/day) can be toxic.
Toledo M, Mostacci B, Bosak M, Jedrzejzak J, Thomas RH, Salas-Puig J, Biraben A, Schmitz B. Expert opinion: use of valproate in girls and women of childbearing potential with epilepsy: recommendations and alternatives based on a review of the literature and clinical experience-a European perspective. J Neurol. 2020 Apr 1. doi: 10.1007/s00415-020-09809-0. Epub ahead of print. PMID: 32239268.</OWLAnnotationProperty5b4bece4_34a5_4955_86ae_fe5305e84ce9>
        <OWLAnnotationProperty70d24189_e686_401a_bf66_f45f9e22e333>在妊娠前一个月和早期妊娠阶段，口服5mg/d大剂量叶酸，可在一定程度上降低胎儿发生先天畸形的风险。
中国医师协会神经内科分会癫(癎)专委会. &quot;妊娠期女性抗癫(癎)药物应用中国专家共识.&quot; 中国医师杂志 17.7(2015):969-971.</OWLAnnotationProperty70d24189_e686_401a_bf66_f45f9e22e333>
        <OWLAnnotationProperty70d24189_e686_401a_bf66_f45f9e22e333>计划妊娠：对癫痫有效控制且可能减停药物的女性癫痫患者，建议在停用AEDs 6个月后可考虑计划妊娠。如果癫痫患者不可能停用药物而计划怀孕，癫痫专科医师应尽量将AEDs调整至单药治疗的低剂量，再建议患者怀孕，并告知如下风险：癫痫发作本身及AEDs均对胎儿有负面影响。如丙戊酸800 mg以上的13剂量可增加胎儿致畸的风险。推荐癫痫女性孕前3个月每天服用叶酸≤5 mg，以减少叶酸代谢相关致胎儿畸形的风险。
&quot;关于成人癫痫患者长程管理的专家共识.&quot; 中华神经科杂志 .07(2013):496-499.</OWLAnnotationProperty70d24189_e686_401a_bf66_f45f9e22e333>
        <OWLAnnotationPropertyd448a312_221a_4215_b2b2_684d470bc1f8>妊娠期和哺乳期补充叶酸对后代6年后的结果积极影响
Treatment with folic acid during pregnancy and breastfeeding has a positive impact on results at 6 years.
Mauri Llerda JA, Suller Marti A, de la Peña Mayor P, Martínez Ferri M, Poza Aldea JJ, Gomez Alonso J, Mercadé Cerdá JM. The Spanish Society of Neurology&apos;s official clinical practice guidelines for epilepsy. Special considerations in epilepsy: comorbidities, women of childbearing age, and elderly patients. Neurologia. 2015 Oct;30(8):510-7. English, Spanish. doi: 10.1016/j.nrl.2014.08.002. Epub 2015 Jan 21. PMID: 25618222.</OWLAnnotationPropertyd448a312_221a_4215_b2b2_684d470bc1f8>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>叶酸</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>A member of the vitamin B family that stimulates the hematopoietic system. It is present in the liver and kidney and is found in mushrooms, spinach, yeast, green leaves, and grasses (POACEAE). Folic acid is used in the treatment and prevention of folate deficiencies and megaloblastic anemia.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>A collective term for pteroylglutamic acids and their oligoglutamic acid conjugates. As a natural water-soluble substance, folic acid is involved in carbon transfer reactions of amino acid metabolism, in addition to purine and pyrimidine synthesis, and is essential for hematopoiesis and red blood cell production. (NCI05)</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NICE_guidance>All women and girls on AEDs should be offered 5 mg per day of folic acid before any possibility of pregnancy.[2004]
所有服用抗癫痫药物的女性在任何可能怀孕的机会前都应每日补充5mg的叶酸。
nice.org.uk/guidance/cg137</untitled-ontology-34:NICE_guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:ROCG_Guidance>All WWE should be advised to take 5 mg/day of folic acid prior to conception and to continue the intake until at least the end of the first trimester to reduce the incidence of major congenital malformation.
建议所有WWE在孕前补充叶酸5mg/d，至少持续到妊娠早期，以减少MCMs发生率。
[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:C] Prepregnancy folic acid 5 mg/day may be helpful in reducing the risk of AED-related cognitive deficits.
【推荐等级：C】孕前补充5mg/d叶酸可能可以降低AEDs相关认知障碍的风险。
https://www.rcog.org.uk/guidance/browse-all-guidance/green-top-guidelines/epilepsy-in-pregnancy-green-top-guideline-no-68/</untitled-ontology-34:ROCG_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>Folic acid dosing:
[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:A]400 micrograms daily for:women with epilepsy not receiving antiepileptic drug treatment
[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:D]5mg daily for:women with epilepsy receiving antiepileptic drug treatment
 [GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:A]5mg daily for:women with epilepsy not on antiepileptic drug treatment, but with a family history of or a previous child with a neural tube defect
 [GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:A]5mg daily for:women with epilepsy not on antiepileptic drug treatment, but with a BMI &gt;30.
关于叶酸剂量：未接受AEDs治疗的女性癫痫患者补充400ug/d（A级推荐）；接受AEDs治疗的女性癫痫患者补充5mg/d（D级推荐）；没有接受AEDs治疗但有神经管缺陷家族史或曾有孩子出现神经管缺陷的女性癫痫患者补充5mg/d（A级推荐）；没有接受AEDs治疗但BMI＞30的女性癫痫患者（A级推荐）。
Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network.Diagnosis and management of epilepsy in adults. SIGN 143. Edinburgh, SIGN, 2015. Available at: www.sign.ac.uk/guidelines/fulltext/143/index.html</untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:C] Women with epilepsy trying to conceive or who present in the first trimester should be advised to take folic acid during this time to reduce the risk of major congenital malformations.
C级推荐：女性癫痫患者在妊娠早期应服用叶酸以降低MCMs风险。
[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:D]  Women receiving sodium valproate should be advised that folic acid supplementation may reduce the rate of spontaneous miscarriage.
D级推荐：接受VPA治疗的妇女补充叶酸可降低自然流产率。
Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network.Diagnosis and management of epilepsy in adults. SIGN 143. Edinburgh, SIGN, 2015. Available at: www.sign.ac.uk/guidelines/fulltext/143/index.html</untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>
