        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>The use of IONIZING RADIATION to treat malignant NEOPLASMS and some benign conditions.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>Treatment of a disease by means of exposure of the target or the whole body to radiation. Radiation therapy is often used as part of curative therapy and occasionally as a component of palliative treatment for cancer. Other uses include total body irradiation prior to transplantation.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
