    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassb57a8d58_f930_4e0f_a3c5_cdfddadd4c4d -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassb57a8d58_f930_4e0f_a3c5_cdfddadd4c4d">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org//Childbearing-ageWomenwithEpilepsyOntology#OWLClass833b1ac6_9bc8_4025_8bc7_4d267961ec74"/>
        <OWLAnnotationPropertyd448a312_221a_4215_b2b2_684d470bc1f8>如果患者生殖内分泌功能障碍与所服用的AEDs有关，应考虑更换另一种AEDs
If the cause of the problem is associated with one AED, an alternative treatment with another AED should be designed.
Mauri Llerda JA, Suller Marti A, de la Peña Mayor P, Martínez Ferri M, Poza Aldea JJ, Gomez Alonso J, Mercadé Cerdá JM. The Spanish Society of Neurology&apos;s official clinical practice guidelines for epilepsy. Special considerations in epilepsy: comorbidities, women of childbearing age, and elderly patients. Neurologia. 2015 Oct;30(8):510-7. English, Spanish. doi: 10.1016/j.nrl.2014.08.002. Epub 2015 Jan 21. PMID: 25618222.</OWLAnnotationPropertyd448a312_221a_4215_b2b2_684d470bc1f8>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>治疗方案调整</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>As AED concentrations may fall during pregnancy, healthcare professionals need to be aware that dosing may need to be increased.
妊娠期AEDs水平可能会下降，可能需要增加药物剂量。
Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network.Diagnosis and management of epilepsy in adults. SIGN 143. Edinburgh, SIGN, 2015. Available at: www.sign.ac.uk/guidelines/fulltext/143/index.html</untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Physician supervision of a patient under a medicare-approved hospice (patient not present) requiring complex and multidisciplinary care modalities involving regular physician development and/or revision of care plans review of subsequent reports of patient status review of laboratory and other studies communication (including telephone calls) with other health care professionals involved in the patients care integration of new information into the medical treatment plan and/or adjustment of medical therapy within a calendar month 30 minutes or more
Hospice care supervision</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Adjustment of treatment plan</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassb5aa8bbe_5cd8_4b37_b94d_1118391b1ba9 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassb5aa8bbe_5cd8_4b37_b94d_1118391b1ba9">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassad1964c4_15b5_4f14_8e8d_54033a3aab06"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>癫痫患者的生活质量-31</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>The 31-item quality of life in epilepsy (QOLIE) inventory—QOLIE-31—is one instrument developed to assess the QOLIE, yielding a composite score from 0 to 100 that represents a person with epilepsy (PWE)&apos;s overall wellness including cognitive impact and social functioning. A higher score indicates a higher self-reported QOLIE. The QOLIE-31 inventory has been translated and validated in various languages spanning many continents.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Quality of life in epilepsy-31</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassb6191fff_f66b_4229_a247_3309fb95be68 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassb6191fff_f66b_4229_a247_3309fb95be68">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass4f03b57f_7e2e_4082_aae5_bfaf82addf62"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>注意缺陷与多动障碍</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>A behavior disorder originating in childhood in which the essential features are signs of developmentally inappropriate inattention, impulsivity, and hyperactivity. Although most individuals have symptoms of both inattention and hyperactivity-impulsivity, one or the other pattern may be predominant. The disorder is more frequent in males than females. Onset is in childhood. Symptoms often attenuate during late adolescence although a minority experience the full complement of symptoms into mid-adulthood. (From DSM-V)</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
