        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>The principle of functional MRI imaging is to take a series of images of an organ in quick succession and to statistically analyze the images for differences among them. Most commonly used in studies of brain function.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
