    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassd60e9389_e868_4ce3_a35e_33e8d0f630d1 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassd60e9389_e868_4ce3_a35e_33e8d0f630d1">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass66ab68e0_1089_40c9_8b6a_99ddbf3b157a"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>与避孕药物有相互作用的抗癫痫药物</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>Antiseizure medications that have drug interactions with oral contraceptives(备注：参考ISBN 978190910344、https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/cg137、https://www.rcog.org.uk/en/guidelines-research-services/guidelines/gtg68/、PMID: 25618222)</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>[GRADES OF RECOMMENDATION:D]  For women receiving hepatic enzyme-inducing antiepileptic drugs:
D级推荐：对于正在接受肝酶诱导AEDs治疗的妇女：
if the antiepileptic drug is withdrawn, it is important to note that enzyme induction persists for up to four weeks. Contraceptive cover should be ensured during this time.
如果停用AEDs，应注意酶诱导作用将持续4周，在这期间应确保避孕措施的有效性。
Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network.Diagnosis and management of epilepsy in adults. SIGN 143. Edinburgh, SIGN, 2015. Available at: www.sign.ac.uk/guidelines/fulltext/143/index.html</untitled-ontology-34:SIGN_Guidance>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Antiseizure medications that have drug interactions with oral contraceptives</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassd75d3dde_3726_43b1_91d6_02fc30c7e388 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassd75d3dde_3726_43b1_91d6_02fc30c7e388">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass27ac4f10_e5b8_47ab_a5f8_c82dfe5fe6f2"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>多塞平</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>A dibenzoxepin tricyclic compound. It displays a range of pharmacological actions including maintaining adrenergic innervation. Its mechanism of action is not fully understood, but it appears to block reuptake of monoaminergic neurotransmitters into presynaptic terminals. It also possesses anticholinergic activity and modulates antagonism of histamine H(1)- and H(2)-receptors.</untitled-ontology-34:MESH_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>A dibenzoxepin derivative and tricyclic antidepressant (TCA) with antipruritic, antidepressive and anxiolytic activities. Doxepin blocks the reuptake of norepinephrine and serotonin (5-HT) into presynaptic terminals thereby prolonging the availability of the monoaminergic neurotransmitters within the synaptic cleft and enhancing their neurotransmission. Doxepin also has antagonistic effects on histamine H1, 5-HT2, alpha-1 adrenergic, and muscarinic receptors. The antipruritic effect of this agent is mediated through inhibition of histamine receptors.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>Doxepin (substance)
Silenor
Doxepin-containing product
1-Propanamine 3-dibenz(be)oxepin-11(6H)-ylidene-NN-dimethyl-
DOXEPIN
Product containing doxepin (medicinal product)
Doxepinum
Doxepina</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Doxepin</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassd7b1ac15_430a_40a9_ba4a_17050b7e1e2a -->

