    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClassee0c1eea_51e2_4896_9d8d_80ae5133fae0">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass6ab90554_6107_4c7c_9c2c_cb7aae95fd96"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>去甲肾上腺素再摄取抑制剂</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>Norepinephrine Reuptake Inhibitors (NRIs) are drugs that function primarily by inhibiting the reuptake of the neurotransmitter norepinephrine (noradrenaline) and/or epinephrine (adrenaline). Inhibiting the reuptake of norepinephrine tends to elicit stimulating effects, thereby increasing both cortical arousal and energy levels. The NRI drugs are typically prescribed to individuals that may benefit from increased arousal such as in cases of ADHD, narcolepsy, and depression</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>NRIs</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


