    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClasseeaebda8_dea2_4dc5_8610_6bd989c7c33d">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/administrator/ontologies/2022/0/untitled-ontology-34#OWLClass9aada549_0c92_4f7e_9ebc_46695086f493"/>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>噻托溴铵</untitled-ontology-34:Chinese>
        <untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>The bromide salt form of tiotropium, a quaternary ammonium derivative of atropine and a muscarinic receptor antagonist, with bronchodilating activity. Although it does not display selectivity for specific muscarinic receptors, on topical application, tiotropium bromide acts mainly on M3 muscarinic receptors located on smooth muscle cells and submucosal glands, preventing smooth muscle contraction and mucus secretion, thus producing a bronchodilatory effect.</untitled-ontology-34:NCIt_Definition>
        <untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>TIOTROPIUM BROMIDE ANHYDROUS
Tiotropium Bromide</untitled-ontology-34:Synonyms>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="zh">Tiotropium Bromide</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


